NXR-101|Modular static configuration|Configuration|The system shall separate mandatory kernel, architecture port, BSP and optional services, with validated target and independent feature profiles generated using C# with XDoc.|Easy configuration must preserve static memory and honest support status.|List targets and minimal/default/diagnostic profiles; deterministic cache generation; invalid identity/capacity/topology fails; OFF Ethernet omits its library; no runtime loading or heap; planned ports fail before compiler selection.|C# configuration tests, supported preset builds and negative CMake profiles.|NXR-002,NXR-076,NXR-078|config/system.json; CMake cache; CPU_COUNT=1 and up initially.|All configured firmware storage fixed before start; configurator catalogue <=1MiB.|config/system.json,tools/NexRT.Configure/Program.cs,cmake/platform.cmake,cmake/modules.cmake|C# profile generation and CMake module boundaries exist; complete future module dependency and ABI gates remain planned.|tools/NexRT.Configure/Program.cs,cmake/platform.cmake,cmake/modules.cmake|tools/NexRT.Configure/Program.cs|PartialSourceUnverified
NXR-102|Architecture port boundary|Architecture|Architecture-specific context construction, interrupt control, trap classification and timer access shall reside in selected architecture ports with explicit frame and ABI contracts.|C++ scheduler code must not embed one ISA's assembly.|Kernel has no inline assembly; RISCue preserves its36-word frame and gp/tp initialization; ports never share incompatible assembly; 64-bit ports replace fixed32-bit context assumptions before support claims.|RV32 cross-build, disassembly/frame review and per-port register canary tests.|NXR-007,NXR-008,NXR-080,NXR-101|Compile-time selected port; no runtime virtual dispatch.|Fixed per-thread frame and per-CPU port state; no heap.|src/kernel.cpp,ports/riscue/rtos_port.hpp,ports/riscue/context.S|RISCue hardware operations extracted; current public context/trap ABI still32-bit and target execution pending.|src/kernel.cpp,ports/riscue/rtos_port.hpp||PartialSourceUnverified
NXR-103|VORAGO Cortex-M target families|Porting|Provisional VORAGO VA108xx Cortex-M0 and VA416xx Cortex-M4 profiles shall require confirmed part/board, separate architecture capabilities and vendor-accurate BSP before firmware enablement.|Virago is interpreted provisionally as VORAGO; family capabilities differ.|Confirm vendor/part; implement vectors, PendSV/SVC, NVIC, timer, startup and linker from selected part documents; configure FP ABI explicitly; unavailable M0 instructions forbidden; EDAC/watchdog fault policy documented; no generic guessed addresses.|Exact-part cross-build plus vector, full register, preemption, fault and noheap target suites.|NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|Separate armv6-m and armv7e-m profiles; soft-float initial unless qualified otherwise.|Vendor SRAM/code map; boot stacks and frames budgeted per part.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst|Vendor research identifies M0/M4 families; exact requested vendor/part awaits confirmation and neither port is implemented.
NXR-104|Zynq-7000 Cortex-A9 target|Porting|The Zynq-7000 ARMv7-A target shall bind a specific board/part, boot handoff, exception mode, GIC, timer and cache/MMU policy before firmware enablement.|Single-core7000S and dual-core7000 are distinct hardware topologies.|Exact memory map and boot-owner contract; preserve all declared register state; FP/NEON disabled or saved under qualified ABI; CPU1 parked for UP; IRQ routing, cache/DMA and noheap tests pass.|Board-specific cross-build, context/IRQ/timer/cache ownership and target qualification.|NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|A9 profile; select exact7000/7000S SKU; UP first.|Boot-reserved DDR/OCM regions, exception stacks and BSP pools; no dynamic allocation.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst|AMD source identifies A9 family and single/dual variants; no A9 context/startup/BSP exists.
NXR-105|Zynq UltraScale R5F target|Porting|The Zynq UltraScale+ Cortex-R5F target shall define split/lockstep mode, TCM map, boot ownership, MPU, interrupt and timer policy before firmware enablement.|Lockstep is one logical execution context rather than SMP.|Selected mode matches firmware/map; CPU count counts logical contexts; TCM/DDR and A53 shared regions partitioned; FP disabled or context-qualified; remote reset and DMA ownership bounded.|R5 board context, timer, fault, TCM, interprocessor visibility and noheap qualification.|NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-110,NXR-111|ARMv7-R; UP initially; AMP separately qualified; no R5 SMP claim.|Static per-image TCM/DDR, IRQ stacks and shared mailbox limits.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst|AMD source identifies R5F subsystem; R5 startup, split/lockstep policy and BSP are not implemented.
NXR-106|Zynq UltraScale A53 target|Porting|The Cortex-A53 target shall provide a separate AArch64 context ABI, exception-level boot contract, GIC, generic timer and cache/MMU policy.|Existing32-bit frame pointers cannot implement64-bit A53 contexts.|Pointer-width-safe public context and assembly offsets verified; chosen EL and firmware handoff explicit; SIMD/FP disabled or fully saved; exact SKU core count enforced; secondary CPUs parked in UP.|AArch64 compile/layout fixtures and exact-board register/timer/interrupt/cache suites.|NXR-080,NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|ARMv8-A AArch64; selected two/four-core part; UP first.|64-bit aligned boot context/exception stacks and explicit reserved memory.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst,include/rtos.hpp|A53 family is researched; current uint32_t context ABI and lack of ARM startup prevent an executable port.
NXR-107|Classic MicroBlaze target|Porting|Classic32-bit MicroBlaze shall have its own generated-hardware-specific port with pinned compiler ABI, endian, vector, cache, timer and interrupt options.|MicroBlaze is neither ARM nor MicroBlaze V RISC-V.|Hardware export hash records multiplier/divider/barrel shifter/FP/cache/endian settings; compiler flags agree; AXI INTC/timer and linker map match design; alignment and prefetch margins respected; V is separate profile.|Hardware/compiler mismatch negatives and context/IRQ/timer/cache/noheap suites.|NXR-085,NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|Exact Vivado hardware design and tool version; single CPU initially.|Static BRAM/DDR sections, exception stack and descriptors from hardware map.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst|AMD documents configurable ISA/ABI and peripherals; no MicroBlaze port/BSP or hardware export is supplied.
NXR-108|Tang Nano9K SoC configuration|Porting|Tang Nano9K support shall bind FPGA bitstream, selected RISC-V core, timer/IRQ/CSR behavior, clocks and memory map rather than infer CPU support from board name.|The board accepts multiple soft cores with incompatible interrupt contracts.|Confirm soft core; RISCue pairing provisional; oscillator not assumed CPU/timer clock; validate synthesized map and timing; custom PicoRV IRQ cannot reuse machine-mode port; PSRAM controller/init and worst-case timing qualified before kernel stack placement.|Bitstream identity, CSR/IRQ/timer and memory timing tests plus board qualification.|NXR-081,NXR-086,NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|Provisional RISCue RV32 profile on Gowin GW1NR-9; board/core selection explicit.|Critical stacks/internal RAM unless external access bounded; no invented MMIO/linker defaults.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst|Sipeed confirms FPGA board and oscillator; selected user's SoC/bitstream remains unknown and board port is planned.
NXR-109|Future homogeneous SMP contract|Multiprocessing|Future SMP shall use statically reserved per-CPU current/idle state and IRQ stacks with cross-CPU synchronization, affinity and remote rescheduling.|Local interrupt masking cannot protect shared scheduler state across CPUs.|Acquire/release publication and bounded spinlocks reviewed; IPIs and deterministic priority/migration policy tested; coherent/noncoherent ownership explicit; global timer and migration metrics defined; no heap; SMP requests rejected until qualified.|Multicore race/model tests, IPI/affinity/migration and cache/conservation stress.|NXR-002,NXR-017,NXR-069,NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|Homogeneous ISA/ABI only; explicit CPU count, affinity and lock policy; disabled initially.|Boot per-CPU stacks/state and fixed shared pools; no online dynamic CPU/thread creation.|src/kernel.cpp,config/system.json,cmake/platform.cmake,docs/platforms.rst|Current global scheduler/current and local IRQ masking are UP-only; configuration rejects SMP rather than implying support.
NXR-110|Future partitioned AMP contract|Multiprocessing|Future AMP shall use independently booted kernel images with partitioned memory, timer/IRQ ownership and bounded shared-memory communication.|Heterogeneous A53/R5/FPGA combinations cannot share one context scheduler.|Image/memory/IRQ owner manifest prevents overlap; boot/reset handshake finite; cache visibility and message ownership explicit; stale reset generations rejected; lockstep counted as one logical CPU; current unsupported AMP rejected.|Dual-image boot/reset, mailbox saturation, cache visibility and isolation tests.|NXR-002,NXR-020,NXR-101,NXR-102,NXR-111|Independent per-ISA static images; fixed mailboxes; AMP disabled initially.|Boot-reserved per-image memory and bounded shared regions; no shared heap.|config/system.json,cmake/platform.cmake,docs/platforms.rst|AMP is the documented initial heterogeneous design direction; no interprocessor boot/mailbox implementation exists.
NXR-111|Architecture-specific port qualification|Verification|Each new architecture/board profile shall remain planned until its exact context ABI, startup, timer, interrupt, memory and ownership evidence is recorded.|Profile files alone do not implement target support.|Correct compiler ELF attributes; all integer and enabled FP/SIMD/TLS state tested; nested IRQ policy, rollover/catch-up, priority, noheap/constructors and stack/link overflow pass; logs bind board/bitstream/image/config; unexecuted cells remain unverified.|Per-port compile/disassembly and exact RTL/board matrix with failure injections.|NXR-082,NXR-083,NXR-084,NXR-086,NXR-094,NXR-101|Explicit architecture/board/configuration matrix; enabled optional state enumerated.|Fixed test stacks/pools and bounded retained evidence per target.|config/system.json,docs/platforms.rst,docs/verification.rst|Only RISCue cross-builds; no new architecture startup/context/driver implementation or board execution evidence exists.
